# What `git archive` leaves out of the module tarball an air-gapped install receives.
#
# `export-ignore` affects `git archive` only. The Terraform Registry and a `git::` or
# `github.com/...?ref=` source fetch the repository itself, so they still see every file.
#
# `git archive <tag>` reads this file as it was at that tag: a tag cut before this file
# existed archives the whole tree, `.github/` included.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#   examples/  - examples/production is the root configuration an operator copies.
#   tests/     - the README cites tests/diagnostic_bundle_test.sh as the proof that the
#                diagnostic bundle carries no secrets; the proof ships with the claim.
#   .gitignore - its `*.tfvars` rule is meant to be copied into the install repo.

# This repository's own CI and docs-pin workflows. They run nothing in an install.
/.github        export-ignore

# Guidance for coding agents working on this repository, not on an install.
/CLAUDE.md      export-ignore

/.gitattributes export-ignore
